---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AuthorReviewerCard from '@/components/editorial/AuthorReviewerCard.astro';
import ContextualLinks from '@/components/seo/ContextualLinks.astro';
import { StructuredDataGenerator } from '@/lib/seo';
import { AuthorManager } from '@/lib/editorial';

const siteUrl = 'https://lic-calculators.com';
const author = AuthorManager.getDefaultAuthor();
const reviewer = AuthorManager.getDefaultReviewer();

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Educational Guides', url: '/guides/' },
  { name: 'LIC Surrender After 10 Years', url: '/guides/lic-surrender-after-10-years' }
];

const articleSchema = StructuredDataGenerator.generateArticle({
  headline: 'Surrendering Your LIC Policy After 10 Years: Value, Loss % & Better Alternatives',
  description: 'At year 10 the surrender loss shrinks a lot versus year 5, but usually does not vanish. An illustrative ₹50,000-a-year example shows the payout, why the paid-up value is often the stronger option now, and how Form 5074 and the 7–15 day NEFT timeline work.',
  url: `${siteUrl}/guides/lic-surrender-after-10-years`,
  publishedDate: '2026-10-21T00:00:00Z',
  modifiedDate: '2026-10-21T00:00:00Z',
  author,
  reviewer
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LIC Surrender After 10 Years: How Much You Get & Lose"
  description="Year-10 surrender value on an illustrative ₹50,000/yr 20-year endowment: ~₹4.6–5.1 lakh back on ₹5 lakh paid. Why the loss band narrows, paid-up vs surrender at year 10, Form 5074 process and NEFT timing."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-10">
    <div class="space-y-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-8">
      <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-brand-50 text-brand-700 border border-brand-200">
        Educational Guide • Surrender Valuation
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        Surrendering Your LIC Policy After 10 Years: Value, Loss &amp; the Paid-Up Alternative
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Ten years in, the surrender maths looks nothing like it did at year five — the guaranteed floor is higher, the special surrender value has caught up with the premiums, and "just stop paying" has become a genuinely strong option. Here is the year-10 picture, priced on one example.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Tool CTA -->
    <div class="bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-900">Compare surrender vs paid-up on your numbers</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-brand-700">Enter your premium, term and years paid to see both the exit value today and the paid-up amount at maturity.</p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="/lic-surrender-loss-calculator/"
        class="px-4 py-2 bg-brand-600 hover:bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-xs rounded-xl transition-colors shrink-0 shadow-sm"
      >
        Compare Your Options &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Guide Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6 text-slate-700">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. The Worked Example: ₹50,000 a Year, 20-Year Endowment</h2>
      <p>
        Take a 20-year endowment with a sum assured of ₹10,00,000 and an annual premium of ₹50,000, paid without a miss for 10 years:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 not-prose">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase block">You have paid</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">₹5,00,000</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Ten annual premiums of ₹50,000 each.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-700 uppercase block">Illustrative payout today</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">≈ ₹4.6–5.1 lakh</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">The higher of GSV and SSV for this profile — roughly 92–102 paise per rupee paid. Only LIC's written quotation fixes your figure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-rose-700 uppercase block">What you permanently give up</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">All future bonuses + cover</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">The remaining 10 years of bonus accrual and the ₹10 lakh life cover end the day you surrender.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Compare the shape with <a href="/guides/lic-surrender-after-5-years/" class="text-brand-700 font-semibold hover:text-brand-800">year 5</a>: there, about 45 paise of every rupee vanished. At year 10 the immediate cash loss is usually small — the real cost has moved to the bonuses and cover you abandon.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Why the Loss Band Narrows by Year 10</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>GSV's floor rises with duration.</strong> The guaranteed surrender value starts at 30% of premiums (excluding the first year) and the applicable factors climb steadily — by years 8–10 traditional plans are typically around the 50% zone of eligible premiums, plus a discounted value of vested bonuses.</li>
        <li><strong>SSV discounts less.</strong> The special surrender value is your paid-up value (paid-up sum assured plus vested bonuses) adjusted for the years left to maturity. With 10 years left instead of 15, the discount shrinks; under the <a href="/guides/lic-irdai-surrender-rules-2024/" class="text-brand-700 font-semibold hover:text-brand-800">post-October-2024 IRDAI method</a>, the SSV is the present value of that paid-up amount at the 10-year G-Sec yield plus up to 50 basis points.</li>
        <li><strong>Vested bonuses are now meaningful.</strong> Ten years of simple reversionary bonuses sit inside both calculations — surrendering throws away their remaining growth, not their accrued value.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. At Year 10, Price Paid-Up Before You Price Surrender</h2>
      <p>
        The paid-up value formula decides the alternative:
      </p>
      <p class="not-prose p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 text-sm">
        <strong>Paid-up sum assured</strong> = 10 paid ÷ 20 payable × ₹10,00,000 = <strong>₹5,00,000</strong>, plus the bonuses already vested — payable at maturity (or earlier death), with no further premiums.
      </p>
      <p>
        Set that beside the surrender cheque: surrender gives roughly the same headline money <em>today</em> but ends the cover and caps everything; paid-up keeps ₹5 lakh of cover running for free and lets time finish the job. At year 5, surrender often won this comparison on need; at year 10, paid-up usually does.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. If You Still Decide to Exit: the Process</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li>Visit the <strong>servicing branch</strong> and take a written surrender quotation (GSV and SSV separately) before signing anything.</li>
        <li>Submit <strong>Form 5074 (Surrender Discharge Voucher)</strong> with the original policy bond, NEFT mandate, cancelled cheque and PAN copy.</li>
        <li>Any outstanding policy loan and interest are adjusted from the payout; the balance is credited to your bank — branches typically complete this within about <strong>7–15 days</strong> of a complete submission.</li>
        <li>Keep the stamped acknowledgement until the credit lands.</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 border-t border-slate-200 pt-4">
        This guide is independent educational content, not LIC or IRDAI advice. GSV factors, SSV method and bonuses vary by plan and issue date; the branch's written surrender quotation for your policy is the only final figure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Links -->
    <ContextualLinks currentPath="/lic-surrender-loss-calculator" />

    <!-- Author & Reviewer Trust Box -->
    <AuthorReviewerCard author={author} reviewer={reviewer} lastReviewedDate="October 2026" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
